<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leon Battista Alberti</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1404">1404</a>–<a href="/years/1472">1472</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leon Battista Alberti was an Italian humanist, architect and writer, one of the founding figures of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> art theory. His treatises On Painting and On the Art of Building set out the principles of perspective and of classical architecture. His buildings include the façade of Santa Maria Novella in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tempio-malatestiano">Tempio Malatestiano</a> in Rimini and Sant'Andrea in Mantua.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leon-battista-alberti.jpg" alt="Leon Battista Alberti" width="320" height="447" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Leon Battista Alberti · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Leon_Battista_Alberti,_Self-Portrait,_c._1435,_NGA_43845.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
